{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Give ear, O heavens.</b> From the word אוזן (ear), meaning: incline your ears. From the preceding passage it continues — 'and I will call as witnesses against them the heavens and the earth' — he said to the witnesses that they should hear the words of testimony." "<b>Give ear, O heavens.</b> For it was before you that I gave you the Torah, as it is said: 'for from the heavens I spoke with you.'" "<b>And may the earth hear.</b> For upon it they stood when they said 'we will do and we will hear.'" "<b>Give ear.</b> Because they are numerous, as our rabbis of blessed memory stated — that they are seven — he used the plural form with them." "<b>And may the earth hear.</b> And the earth is singular, so he used the singular form with it." "<b>Give ear, O heavens, and hear, O earth.</b> Concerning this was said: \"Hear, O heavens, and give ear, O earth, for HaShem has spoken.\" Moses our teacher was at that moment far from the heavens and standing on the earth; therefore he gave האזנה to the heavens, for it is customary to say to one who stands far in the language of האזנה, that he incline his ear to hear because he is far. And he gave שמיעה to the earth, for one does not say to one who is close in the language of האזנה but in the language of שמיעה. But Isaiah, who was speaking in the name of HaShem, gave שמיעה to the heavens and האזנה to the earth. And one may say the reverse: האזנה is applicable where one is close, and שמיעה where one is far. Moses, whose habit was in heaven, said <b>Give ear, O heavens</b> — for they were close to him — <b>and hear, O earth</b>, which was far from him. Isaiah came and said the opposite: \"Hear, O heavens,\" which were far from him, \"and give ear, O earth,\" which was close to him.\"" "<b>The heavens.</b> The host of the heavens." "<b>And the earth.</b> The host of the earth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {5 "The second interpretation (וי״מ למפרע) presents the reverse logic but concludes that Moses and Isaiah actually said the same thing, each from his own perspective of proximity."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:05.437651433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}